course: dictionary
lesson: 6698
title: Meet the ocelot
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An ocelot is a wild cat. It is about twice the size of a pet cat, and its fur is covered in spots and stripes.
explain: Ocelots live in the forests of Central and South America. They are wild animals, not pets.
explain: Look at the brackets in «The giant armadillo can dig a big burrow in a night, and lizards, ocelots (small wild cats) and birds later shelter in it.» The brackets tell you that an ocelot is a small wild cat. Writers often explain a hard word like this right next to it.
fact: An ocelot is a wild cat about twice the size of a pet cat.
fact: Ocelots have spotted and striped fur.
fact: Ocelots live in the forests of Central and South America.
fact: Ocelots hunt at night.
fact: Ocelot is a noun: one ocelot, two ocelots.
exercise: «The giant armadillo can dig a big burrow in a night, and lizards, ocelots (small wild cats) and birds later shelter in it.» What is an ocelot? | *A small wild cat | A bird that digs burrows | A pet cat from a city home | A kind of lizard
exercise: What is the plural of ocelot? | *ocelots | ocelotes | ocelotties | ocelot's
exercise: Ocelots are wild cats that hunt at night. Which word tells you when they hunt? | *night | forests | wild | cats
test: Where do ocelots live? | *Forests of Central and South America | Icy mountains of the Arctic | Deserts of Africa
test: An ocelot is about how big compared with a pet cat? | Half the size | Ten times the size | *About twice the size
exam: Which fact about ocelots is true? | *They have spotted and striped fur | They are kept as farm animals | They have plain grey fur | They live in the Arctic
